<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
<h2>What Makes the FlameThrower Stackburger Different</h2>
  <p>The FlameThrower® gets its heat from two sources working together: fresh jalapeños and DQ's proprietary FlameThrower sauce. The sauce is a creamy-spicy blend with a building kick that develops progressively with each bite. Pepper Jack cheese adds a mild dairy heat that amplifies both. The result is a burger that is noticeably spicy without being painful — the kind of heat that food fans enjoy rather than endure. Find the FlameThrower and every other DQ item on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>
  <h2>FlameThrower vs. Other DQ Burgers</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Burger</th><th>Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Heat Level</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>FlameThrower® Stackburger</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$10.87</td><td>780</td><td>🌶️🌶️🌶️ Bold spicy</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Backyard Bacon Ranch Stackburger</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$9.99</td><td>730</td><td>🌶️ Mild (ranch)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Loaded A.1.® Steakhouse Burger</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$10.49</td><td>760</td><td>🌶️ Mild (A.1. sauce)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Original Cheeseburger</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$6.39</td><td>400</td><td>None</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h2>Who Should Order the FlameThrower?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Order the FlameThrower if:</strong> You enjoy spicy food, want the boldest burger on the DQ menu, or are a regular who wants something more interesting than the standard lineup.</li>
    <li><strong>Skip it if:</strong> You are heat-sensitive, ordering for kids, or prefer classic flavors. The Original Cheeseburger ($6.39) or Backyard Bacon Ranch ($9.99) are better choices.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>The FlameThrower Stackburger — Full Breakdown</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Beef patty</strong> — 100% real seasoned beef, never frozen, cooked to order</li>
    <li><strong>Pepper Jack cheese</strong> — Mild heat from the cheese itself</li>
    <li><strong>FlameThrower sauce</strong> — Creamy, spicy, building heat — DQ's proprietary blend</li>
    <li><strong>Fresh jalapeños</strong> — Sliced fresh, adds texture and direct heat</li>
    <li><strong>Lettuce and tomato</strong> — Cool, fresh crunch that tempers the heat slightly</li>
    <li><strong>Mayo</strong> — Adds creaminess and helps balance the spice</li>
    <li><strong>Toasted bun</strong> — Sturdy enough to hold all the toppings</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is the FlameThrower Stackburger very spicy?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The FlameThrower has moderate to bold heat from jalapeños and FlameThrower sauce. It builds progressively — not overwhelming for most spice fans, but clearly spicy. If you are heat-sensitive, choose the Backyard Bacon Ranch Stackburger instead.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How much is the double FlameThrower?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The Double FlameThrower Stackburger is approximately $13.49, though pricing varies by location. It adds a second beef patty and increases the calorie count to approximately 1,020 calories.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What is in the FlameThrower sauce?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The FlameThrower sauce is a proprietary DQ blend. It is a creamy, spicy sauce similar to a chipotle mayo in texture with a building heat profile. The exact recipe is not publicly disclosed.</div></div></div></div>
  <p style="margin-top:32px;">For the complete DQ menu including all categories and deals, visit <a href="/"><strong>The Queen Dairy Menu</strong></a>.</p>
